dabsite for Debian/Ubuntu
=========================

Layout
  /opt/dabsite/app/               the app (bin, src, migrations, static)
  /opt/dabsite/bin/scm            the dabscm runtime it was built with
  /opt/dabsite/VERSION            package version, commit, dabscm version
  /etc/dabsite/config.scm         the config (created on first install,
                                  never overwritten; root:dabsite 0640)
  /etc/default/dabsite            optional: JAVA_OPTS="-Xmx512m"
  /var/lib/dabsite/files          uploaded files (content-addressed)
  /usr/bin/dabsite-admin          runs a tool from app/bin, e.g.
                                    dabsite-admin hash-passphrase 'passphrase'
                                    dabsite-admin gen-passphrase

Services
  dabsite.service                 the web app (127.0.0.1:8088 by default)
  dabsite-health.timer            probes /healthz every minute, restarts
                                  the app after two failures
  dabsite-restart.timer           daily restart at 04:00

First install
  1. PostgreSQL user and database:
       sudo -u postgres createuser -P dabsite
       sudo -u postgres createdb -O dabsite dabsite
  2. Edit /etc/dabsite/config.scm: db-password (and db-user/db-name if
     different), auth-passphrase-hash from
       dabsite-admin hash-passphrase 'your passphrase'
     cookie-secret is already filled with a fresh random secret.
  3. sudo systemctl start dabsite dabsite-health.timer dabsite-restart.timer
     The schema migrations run on start: journalctl -u dabsite -f
  4. Reverse proxy with TLS in front of 127.0.0.1:8088: see
     nginx.conf.example / apache.conf.example in this directory. Keep the
     login and poll rate limits, limit_conn and the client timeouts.

The services start automatically on install and upgrade once no setting in
the config holds "change-me" or a REPLACE_WITH_... placeholder.

Moving an existing installation (/home/dab/www/dabsite, user dab)
  1. Stop and remove the old units; units in /etc/systemd/system would
     shadow the packaged ones:
       sudo systemctl disable --now dabsite.service dabsite-health.timer dabsite-restart.timer
       sudo rm /etc/systemd/system/dabsite*.service /etc/systemd/system/dabsite*.timer
       sudo systemctl daemon-reload
  2. sudo apt install ./dabsite_<version>_all.deb
  3. Copy db-*, auth-passphrase-hash, cookie-secret (keeps logins valid),
     cookie-name and default-site-lang from the old config.scm into
     /etc/dabsite/config.scm. Keep files-dir "/var/lib/dabsite/files" and
     secure-cookies? #t.
  4. Copy the uploaded files:
       sudo cp -a /home/dab/www/dabsite/data/files/. /var/lib/dabsite/files/
       sudo chown -R dabsite:dabsite /var/lib/dabsite/files
  5. sudo systemctl start dabsite dabsite-health.timer dabsite-restart.timer
  The database stays as it is; the app connects with the credentials from
  the config, not as the system user.

Upgrades
  sudo apt install ./dabsite_<newer>_all.deb restarts the services; the
  config and the data are kept.

Removal
  apt remove keeps /etc/dabsite and /var/lib/dabsite; apt purge removes
  the config but still keeps the data and the database.

Memory
  The JVM takes 1/4 of the RAM by default. Set JAVA_OPTS="-Xmx512m" (or
  what fits) in /etc/default/dabsite.
